        <body>
            <div xml:id="d747">

                <pb facs="0709" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg611"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-04-14"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 14, 1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 302.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your instruction 314, of
                    the 21st February last, respecting Messrs. Peabody &amp; Co.’s shipments on the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Mashona</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Maria</hi>,
                    I have the honor to inclose herewith copies of a note from Mr. White to Lord
                    Salisbury in relation thereto, and of the reply from the foreign office, which I
                    have just received.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>



